IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `iana-types`
IMPORT `iana-employment`

-- Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) — GOAL 2: THE CIVIL
-- PENALTY (ss 15(2)-(6), 16, 17(4A)-(4E)).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-2006-13.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — the civil penalty`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- s 15(2) "The Secretary of State may give an employer who acts contrary to
-- this section a notice requiring him to pay a penalty of a specified amount
-- not exceeding the prescribed maximum." (5): without first establishing
-- whether (3) applies.
@ref s 15(2), (5)
@export Whether the Secretary of State may give a penalty notice under s 15(2) of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): the employer acted contrary to s 15, and the amount specified does not exceed the prescribed maximum (whether the s 15(3) excuse applies need not be established first, s 15(5)). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`  @desc The employment and the employee's immigration position
      p IS A `Penalty facts`      @desc The prescribed maximum and the amount specified
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a penalty notice may be given for` e `with` p IF
        `the employment is contrary to s 15 in` e
    AND p's `the amount specified` AT MOST p's `the prescribed maximum`

-- s 15(3) "An employer is excused from paying a penalty if he shows that he
-- complied with any prescribed requirements in relation to the employment."
-- (4) "But the excuse in subsection (3) shall not apply to an employer who
-- knew, at any time during the period of the employment, that it was contrary
-- to this section."
@ref s 15(3)-(4)
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is excused under s 15(3) by` p IF
        p's `complied with the prescribed requirements`
    AND NOT (p's `knew at any time that the employment was contrary to s 15`)

@ref ss 15(2)-(4), 16(4)(a)
@export The penalty an employer must pay under s 15 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): the amount specified, if a notice may be given, the employer is not excused (compliance with the prescribed requirements, unless it knew the employment was contrary to s 15) and the penalty was not cancelled on objection; otherwise 0. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN e IS AN `Employment facts`  @desc The employment and the employee's immigration position
      p IS A `Penalty facts`      @desc The requirements complied with, knowledge, the amounts, and the objection outcome
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the penalty payable for` e `with` p MEANS
    IF       `a penalty notice may be given for` e `with` p
         AND NOT (`the employer is excused under s 15(3) by` p)
         AND NOT cancelled
    THEN p's `the amount specified`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        cancelled MEANS
            CONSIDER p's `objection`
            WHEN `penalty cancelled` THEN TRUE
            OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 15(6)(c): the notice must "specify a date, at least 28 days after the
-- date specified in the notice as the date on which it is given, before which
-- the penalty must be paid".
@ref s 15(6)(c)
@export The earliest pay-by date a penalty notice under s 15 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK) may specify: 28 days after the date the notice states as the date it is given. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc The date the notice states as the date it is given
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest pay-by date for` p MEANS
    `the day` 28 `days after` (p's `notice states it is given on`)

-- s 17(4A) "An appeal may be brought only if the employer has given a notice
-- of objection under section 16 and the Secretary of State— (a) has
-- determined the objection by issuing ... the penalty notice (as a result of
-- increasing the penalty ...), (b) has determined the objection by— (i)
-- reducing the penalty ..., or (ii) taking no action ..., or (c) has not
-- informed the employer of a decision before the end of the period". (4B) "An
-- appeal must be brought within the period of 28 days beginning with the
-- relevant date." (4C)-(4E): the date of the new notice, of the decision
-- notice, or the end of the period. The period ends on the relevant date +
-- 27. NOTHING: no appeal may be brought.
@ref s 17(4A)-(4E)
@export The last day for an employer to appeal to the court against a penalty under s 17 of the Immigration, Asylum and Nationality Act 2006 (UK): the end of the 28 days beginning with the relevant date — the date of the new penalty notice (increase), of the notice of decision (reduction or no action), or the end of the period for a decision when none was given; NOTHING where no appeal may be brought (no objection, or the penalty was cancelled). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Penalty facts`  @desc The outcome of the employer's objection and its date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to appeal for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `objection`
    WHEN `no objection given` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `penalty cancelled` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `penalty increased by a new notice given on` d THEN JUST (`the day` 27 `days after` d)
    WHEN `penalty reduced or no action, decision given on` d THEN JUST (`the day` 27 `days after` d)
    WHEN `no decision, the period ended on` d THEN JUST (`the day` 27 `days after` d)
